{"id": "EUVD-2026-86173", "enisaUuid": "162087a5-2788-319c-ae61-8618169bc8f0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: preserve VFS inherited POSIX ACL mask\n\nThe VFS initializes a child's POSIX ACL from the parent's default ACL and\nthe requested creation mode. Do not mutate the parent ACL or overwrite the\nchild's VFS-computed access and default ACLs afterwards.\n\nThis preserves restrictive ACL_MASK entries and prevents SMB object creation\nfrom widening effective permissions.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:57:21", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a19bb1c45667f5a5f6eff9cf6648e0f692d046f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/591acf171644de590cda245fd8595b473a1beb70", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0093909becbda22b62b39b654dbc607faed59cd0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e148e567a9252643baa125cb65d7ae9c2c6cf68a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h69q-mp6v-qjfh", "CVE-2026-93786"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0286b373-20f0-3d7e-a751-31bed24f49b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "1415c124-45cb-3709-b363-18f98d0cbea2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f44158485826c076335d6860d35872271a83791d <e148e567a9252643baa125cb65d7ae9c2c6cf68a"}, {"id": "167eee84-ea46-36d2-b643-9c5e289fb138", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f44158485826c076335d6860d35872271a83791d <4a19bb1c45667f5a5f6eff9cf6648e0f692d046f"}, {"id": "2ea159c5-80ee-30c1-a014-21abaf8f9788", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "43726944-8dc1-319b-b4a4-4335ee95d329", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f44158485826c07633